what's the story with a bitcoin etf  [Music]  bitcoin has arrived on main street with  the launch of a u.s exchange traded fund  that matters because it opens up what  was once a very niche investment to a  much wider pool of potential buyers  you no longer need an account with a  special cryptocurrency exchange or a  futures trading venue  now anyone with a brokerage account can  get price exposure  there's been a lot of excitement in the  weeks immediately following the launch  the market cap of the fund shot to 1.3  billion dollars  what's more this is unlikely to be the  last etf tracking the price of bitcoin  but you really need to read the fine  print  when you put money in a gold etf  custodians go out and buy actual  physical bars and put them in a vault  that creates demand for gold and the  price rises  that's not the case with the current  crop of u.s bitcoin products  instead the sec has decided to approve  only products backed by cash settled  futures contracts  for now at least  in other words the assets that link the  price of the fund to that of bitcoin are  futures contracts which themselves  aren't settled in actual bitcoin but  rather in cash  that has two rather big implications for  the bullish investors  number one demand is transferred away  from actual bitcoin to futures contracts  and unlike bitcoin the supply of futures  contracts is potentially infinite  and number two  rolling the futures contract forward  from one month to the next means that it  is likely to substantially underperform  bitcoin when crypto is rallying which  means that the lineup of crypto etfs  likely to emerge in the us will be more  like trading vehicles and less suitable  for the buy and hold bitcoin bull or the  hodlers as they called  this is decrypted i'm eddie van der walt  lurking in the shadows as producer  matthew long for more content like this  follow us on your favorite platforms
 

